---
title = "How to create a directory"
meta_title = "How to create a directory in Gleam"
subtitle = "using simplifile"
description = "The simplifile package provides file system functionality that works with Gleam on both Erlang and JavaScript"
---

The `simplifile` package provides file-system functions that work on both the
Erlang and JavaScript targets. Add it as a dependency to your package:

```cli
gleam add simplifile
```

Use the [`simplfile.create_directory`](https://simplifile.hexdocs.pm/simplifile.html#create_directory)
function to create a directory.

```gleam
import simplifile.{type FileError}

pub fn main() -> Result(Nil, FileError) {
  simplifile.create_directory("pokemon-cards")
}
```

The containing directory must already exist and there must not already be a
directory at the given location, otherwise an error will be returned.

If you want to ensure a directory and all of its parent directories exist then
you can use the [`simplfile.create_directory_all`](https://simplifile.hexdocs.pm/simplifile.html#create_directory_all)
function instead.

```gleam
import simplifile.{type FileError}

pub fn main() -> Result(Nil, FileError) {
  simplifile.create_directory_all("pokemon/generation-1/fire-type")
}
```

If a directory cannot be created for any reason then these functions will
return a [`simplifile.FileError`](https://simplifile.hexdocs.pm/simplifile.html#FileError).

::: alert-warning
### Files and web browsers

For security reasons web browsers do not let code directly access files, so if
your program runs in browser you will need to use a different approach.

:::
